@startuml tropical-semiring-algebra
' D17 — Tropical semiring algebra panel.
' Depicts: the (min, +) algebra duallity computes in, its two identities, and the consequence that
' a shortest path is the best answer. Mathematical labels are typeset with <latex> (JLaTeXMath).
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #34495E
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}
title D17 · The tropical <latex>(\min, +)</latex> semiring   <latex>\mathbb{K} = (\mathbb{R} \cup \{+\infty\},\, \min,\, +,\, +\infty,\, 0)</latex>

rectangle "<latex>\oplus \;=\; \min</latex>\nthe best (cheapest)\nalternative wins\n\nexample:  <latex>2 \oplus 5 = 2</latex>" as PLUS #FCF3CF
rectangle "⊗ <latex>\;=\; +</latex>\ncosts add up\nalong a path\n\nexample:  2 ⊗ <latex>5 = 7</latex>" as TIMES #FCF3CF
rectangle "<latex>\bar{0} \;=\; +\infty</latex>\nidentity for <latex>\oplus</latex>\n(no path / forbidden)\n\nTropicalWeight::zero()" as ZERO #F2F3F4
rectangle "<latex>\bar{1} \;=\; 0</latex>\nidentity for ⊗\n(a free step)\n\nTropicalWeight::one()" as ONE #F9E79F

PLUS -[hidden]right- TIMES
ZERO -[hidden]right- ONE
PLUS -[hidden]down- ZERO
TIMES -[hidden]down- ONE

note bottom
  Under <latex>(\min, +)</latex>: the <latex>\oplus</latex>-sum over all paths becomes the <b>minimum-cost path</b>,
  and the ⊗-product along a path becomes the <b>sum of edge costs</b>.
  So a shortest path <b>is</b> the best correction.
  ⚠ Naming: <b>zero()</b> is the value <latex>+\infty</latex> and <b>one()</b> is the value <latex>0</latex>.
end note
@enduml
